# BRIDGING

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Bridging is a foundational ground movement designed to develop explosive hip extension, spinal control and positional escape ability during ground fighting.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the fundamental movement patterns for grappling and self-defense.

---

# Philosophy

The bridge is not merely an exercise.

It is one of the primary methods by which athletes create space, reverse position and generate force from the ground.

CAS develops Bridging as a universal combat movement rather than a simple conditioning drill.

